Title: Night Shift
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample fixture (tv-pilot profile; defects injected on purpose)
Contact: fixture@example.com

FADE IN:

COLD OPEN

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - AMBULANCE BAY - NIGHT

Rain off the canopy. PRIYA OKONKWO (30s), scrubs under a parka, meets a
gurney at the doors.

PARAMEDIC
Forty-one, unrestrained, GCS twelve and dropping.

PRIYA
Trauma two. Now.

END OF COLD OPEN

ACT ONE

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - TRAUMA TWO - NIGHT

Priya works. HAROLD VANCE (50s), attending, watches from the doorway
with his arms folded.

HAROLD
You called it before the scan.

PRIYA
I called it before the scan and I was right.

HAROLD
Those are two different sentences.

Priya peels her gloves.

PRIYA
Not tonight they aren't.

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Harold catches up with her at the lifts.

HAROLD
The board meets Thursday.

PRIYA
Let them meet.

HAROLD
They'll ask me whether you're teachable.

PRIYA
Tell them I'm employed.

The lift takes her.

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Priya sits with her boots off. She reads a letter, folds it, puts it in
the locker instead of her bag.

END OF ACT ONE

ACT TWO

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - NURSES' STATION - NIGHT

DELIA MBEKI (40s), charge nurse, drops a chart on the counter.

DELIA
Your trauma two is asking for you.

PRIYA
He's sedated.

DELIA
He's asking anyway.

Priya takes the chart.

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S - TRAUMA TWO - LATER

Priya sits with the patient. Delia watches through the glass.

DELIA
She does this every shift.

HAROLD
I know.

DELIA
And you let her.

HAROLD
I know that too.

END OF ACT TWO

FADE OUT.
